---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import SubNav from '../../components/SubNav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Black Ops 3 GSC Deep Dive — Boink Brands"
  description="The definitive 2026 deep dive into Treyarch's Game Script Code for Black Ops III. Syntax reference, WaW migration, tutorials, ecosystem analysis, and toolchain evolution."
>
  <Header />
  <SubNav activeTab="" />

  <!-- ── Hero ── -->
  <section class="bg-void relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top,rgba(230,0,18,0.18)_0%,transparent_62%)]"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(255,255,255,0.02)_1px,transparent_1px)] bg-[size:36px_36px] opacity-20"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-[var(--width-content)] mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
      <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-accent mb-3">Interactive Guide</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl uppercase leading-none tracking-tight mb-4">
        <span class="text-gradient">Black Ops 3</span>
        <br />
        <span class="text-text-primary">Mod Tools GSC</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm md:text-base max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        The definitive 2026 deep dive into Treyarch&apos;s Game Script Code. Explore the architecture,
        port legacy WaW scripts seamlessly, and master modern development toolchains. Covers syntax reference,
        migration pitfalls, the content ecosystem, and the current state of the BO3 modding scene.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mt-8 max-w-4xl">
        <div class="bo3-stat">
          <p class="bo3-stat-label">WaW Compatibility</p>
          <p class="bo3-stat-value">85% core logic ports verbatim</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bo3-stat">
          <p class="bo3-stat-label">Script Architecture</p>
          <p class="bo3-stat-value">Server GSC + Client CSC airgap</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bo3-stat">
          <p class="bo3-stat-label">Toolchain Status</p>
          <p class="bo3-stat-value">Active in 2026 post-Arxan update</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chrome-divider"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Main Content Grid ── -->
  <section class="bg-obsidian py-8 md:py-10">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--width-content)] mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[260px_1fr] gap-6">

        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <aside class="surface-card rounded-sm p-3 lg:sticky lg:top-6 lg:self-start h-fit">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-text-muted font-bold px-3 pb-2">Sections</p>
          <nav id="bo3-nav" class="space-y-1">
            <a href="#exec-summary" class="bo3-nav-link is-active">Executive Summary</a>
            <a href="#syntax-ref" class="bo3-nav-link">Syntax Reference</a>
            <a href="#waw-compat" class="bo3-nav-link">WaW Compatibility</a>
            <a href="#migration" class="bo3-nav-link">Migration Guide</a>
            <a href="#roadmap" class="bo3-nav-link">Tutorials &amp; Roadmap</a>
            <a href="#ecosystem" class="bo3-nav-link">Content Ecosystem</a>
            <a href="#resources" class="bo3-nav-link">Resources Appendix</a>
            <a href="#state-2026" class="bo3-nav-link">Current State 2026</a>
          </nav>

          <div class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-border space-y-3">
            <div class="bo3-side-note">
              <p class="bo3-side-note-label">Scope</p>
              <p class="bo3-side-note-copy">Covers server-side GSC, client-side CSC, and the WaW-to-BO3 migration path with code comparisons.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bo3-side-note">
              <p class="bo3-side-note-label">Format</p>
              <p class="bo3-side-note-copy">Radar chart ecosystem analysis, collapsible learning roadmap, tabbed migration deep-dive, and inline code blocks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- Main Content -->
        <main id="bo3-content" class="space-y-6">

          <!-- ── 1. Executive Summary ── -->
          <section id="exec-summary" data-guide-section class="surface-card rounded-sm p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24">
            <p class="section-kicker">Executive Summary</p>
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl uppercase text-text-primary leading-none mb-4">Game Script Code Architecture</h2>
            <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
              Game Script Code (GSC) is the foundational, server-side logic execution environment for Call of Duty: Black Ops III.
              Utilizing a syntax derivative of C/C++, it executes on a custom Virtual Machine tied directly to the engine&apos;s 20Hz tick rate.
              It excels at game-state manipulation, entity management, and event-driven architecture via a cooperative multitasking model.
            </p>

            <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl uppercase text-text-primary mb-4">Legacy WaW Core Logic Compatibility</h3>
              <div class="flex justify-between items-end mb-2">
                <span class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary">Standard loops, math, and threading structures</span>
                <span class="text-accent font-mono text-xl font-bold">85%</span>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full bg-ash rounded-full h-4 overflow-hidden">
                <div class="bg-accent h-4 rounded-full" style="width: 85%"></div>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">Despite an 8-year engine gap and 64-bit overhaul, 85% of standard loops, mathematical logic, and threading structures port completely verbatim from World at War to BO3.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-6 border-l-2 border-accent bg-accent/10 p-4">
              <h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Key Takeaway</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary mt-2 leading-relaxed">
                GSC is not just code — it is the nervous system of the engine. Understanding its cooperative threading model and entity referencing system is essential before writing any custom zombies or multiplayer logic.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ── 2. Full Syntax Reference ── -->
          <section id="syntax-ref" data-guide-section class="surface-card rounded-sm p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24">
            <p class="section-kicker">Syntax Reference</p>
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl uppercase text-text-primary leading-none mb-4">Full GSC Syntax Reference</h2>
            <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
              GSC is dynamically typed and relies heavily on implicit entity referencing and asynchronous threading. Below is the core lexical structure required for BO3.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                <p class="mini-kicker">Fundamentals</p>
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl uppercase text-text-primary mb-3">Data Types &amp; Scoping</h3>
                <ul class="guide-list text-sm font-mono">
                  <li><span class="text-blue-400">Int</span>: 1, 52, 97</li>
                  <li><span class="text-blue-400">Float</span>: 5.1754, 0.05</li>
                  <li><span class="text-blue-400">String</span>: &quot;shootable_teddy&quot;</li>
                  <li><span class="text-blue-400">Bool</span>: true (1), false (0)</li>
                  <li><span class="text-blue-400">Array</span>: Zero-indexed dynamic lists</li>
                  <li><span class="text-blue-400">Entity (ent)</span>: Pointers to 3D map objects</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-border">
                  <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary"><strong class="text-text-primary">Local:</strong> <code class="gsc-inline-code">var = 1;</code> (Confined to function)</p>
                  <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-2"><strong class="text-text-primary">Global:</strong> <code class="gsc-inline-code">level.var = 1;</code> (Engine-wide)</p>
                  <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-2"><strong class="text-text-primary">Entity Prop:</strong> <code class="gsc-inline-code">self.var = 1;</code> (Attached to self)</p>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                <p class="mini-kicker">Concurrency</p>
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl uppercase text-text-primary mb-3">Threading &amp; Event Model</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3">GSC operates on cooperative threading. Scripts must manually yield control to the engine to prevent fatal crashes.</p>
                <pre class="guide-code-block"><code><span class="gsc-keyword">wait</span><span class="gsc-plain">(0.05);</span>
<span class="gsc-comment">// Yields execution for exactly 1 server frame.</span>

<span class="gsc-entity">self</span> <span class="gsc-keyword">waittill</span><span class="gsc-plain">("event_name");</span>
<span class="gsc-comment">// Pauses thread until event is broadcast.</span>

<span class="gsc-entity">self</span> <span class="gsc-keyword">notify</span><span class="gsc-plain">("event_name", data);</span>
<span class="gsc-comment">// Broadcasts event and optional data payload.</span>

<span class="gsc-entity">self</span> <span class="gsc-keyword">endon</span><span class="gsc-plain">("death");</span>
<span class="gsc-comment">// Kills thread if entity dies (memory leak prevention).</span></code></pre>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ── 3. WaW Compatibility ── -->
          <section id="waw-compat" data-guide-section class="surface-card rounded-sm p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24">
            <p class="section-kicker">WaW Compatibility</p>
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl uppercase text-text-primary leading-none mb-4">What Still Works 100% From WaW</h2>
            <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
              The 85% compatibility rating means legacy scripts can often be copy-pasted directly into a BO3 environment, provided you add the <code class="gsc-inline-code">function</code> keyword prefix.
            </p>

            <div class="space-y-4">
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm overflow-hidden bg-charcoal/20">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-center px-5 py-3 bg-charcoal/40 border-b border-border">
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-text-secondary">Basic UI Printing &amp; Math</span>
                  <span class="text-xs font-bold text-green-400 uppercase tracking-wider">100% Identical</span>
                </div>
                <pre class="guide-code-block !border-0 !rounded-none"><code><span class="gsc-keyword">function</span> <span class="gsc-function">example_function</span>() {'{'}
    <span class="gsc-entity">iprintlnbold</span>(<span class="gsc-plain">"This is an example function"</span>);
    teddys_to_shoot = <span class="gsc-literal">3</span>;
    <span class="gsc-entity">iprintlnbold</span>( <span class="gsc-plain">"You have "</span> + teddys_to_shoot + <span class="gsc-plain">" Teddy Bears to Shoot"</span> );
{'}'}</code></pre>
              </article>

              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm overflow-hidden bg-charcoal/20">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-center px-5 py-3 bg-charcoal/40 border-b border-border">
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-text-secondary">Event-Driven Infinite Loops</span>
                  <span class="text-xs font-bold text-green-400 uppercase tracking-wider">100% Identical</span>
                </div>
                <pre class="guide-code-block !border-0 !rounded-none"><code><span class="gsc-keyword">function</span> <span class="gsc-function">blood_splatter</span>() {'{'}
    <span class="gsc-entity">self</span> <span class="gsc-keyword">endon</span>( <span class="gsc-plain">"death"</span> );
    <span class="gsc-keyword">while</span>(<span class="gsc-literal">1</span>) {'{'}
        <span class="gsc-entity">self</span> <span class="gsc-keyword">waittill</span>( <span class="gsc-plain">"splatter_blood_on_screen"</span> );
        <span class="gsc-entity">iprintlnbold</span>( <span class="gsc-plain">"splatter blood now"</span> );
    {'}'}
{'}'}</code></pre>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ── 4. Migration & Changes ── -->
          <section id="migration" data-guide-section class="surface-card rounded-sm p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24">
            <p class="section-kicker">Migration Guide</p>
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl uppercase text-text-primary leading-none mb-4">What Changed &amp; Migration Guide</h2>
            <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
              While core logic is identical, the structural paradigm of the engine evolved significantly. BO3 enforces strict compiler rules and networks visuals differently.
            </p>

            <!-- Tabs -->
            <div class="border-b border-border mb-6">
              <nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 -mb-px" aria-label="Migration topic tabs">
                <button type="button" class="migration-tab is-active" data-tab-btn data-target="tab-rules">Strict Rules</button>
                <button type="button" class="migration-tab" data-tab-btn data-target="tab-csc">Server vs Client</button>
                <button type="button" class="migration-tab" data-tab-btn data-target="tab-ui">LUI vs .menu</button>
              </nav>
            </div>

            <div id="tab-rules" class="tab-panel space-y-4">
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                <p class="mini-kicker">Syntax Strictness &amp; Crash Handling</p>
                <ul class="guide-list">
                  <li><strong class="text-text-primary">The <code class="gsc-inline-code">function</code> keyword:</strong> You MUST prepend <code class="gsc-inline-code">function</code> to all definitions. WaW allowed <code class="gsc-inline-code">main() {'{ }'}</code>. BO3 requires <code class="gsc-inline-code">function main() {'{ }'}</code>.</li>
                  <li><strong class="text-text-primary">Fatal Infinite Loops:</strong> In WaW, forgetting a <code class="gsc-inline-code">wait</code> in a <code class="gsc-inline-code">while(1)</code> caused severe lag. In BO3, it immediately causes a fatal <strong>&quot;Connection Interrupted&quot;</strong> server crash.</li>
                  <li><strong class="text-text-primary">Array Iteration Update:</strong> BO3 natively introduces the <code class="gsc-inline-code">foreach</code> loop. You no longer need to write verbose <code class="gsc-inline-code">for(i=0; i&lt;array.size; i++)</code> blocks.</li>
                </ul>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div id="tab-csc" class="tab-panel hidden">
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                <p class="mini-kicker">The Client-Side Script (.csc) Airgap</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
                  WaW processed everything on the server. BO3 separates logic. Server-side scripts (<code class="gsc-inline-code font-mono text-accent">.gsc</code>) handle game logic. Client-side scripts (<code class="gsc-inline-code font-mono text-accent">.csc</code>) handle visual effects, sounds, and thermal states independently per player to save bandwidth.
                </p>
                <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-4 bg-charcoal/40 border-border-light">
                  <p class="text-sm font-mono text-text-muted"><span class="text-text-primary font-bold">Bridge mechanism:</span> ClientFields.</p>
                  <pre class="guide-code-block mt-3"><code><span class="gsc-comment">// Server (.gsc)</span>
<span class="gsc-entity">clientfield</span>::<span class="gsc-keyword">set</span>(<span class="gsc-plain">"show_fx"</span>, <span class="gsc-literal">1</span>);

<span class="gsc-comment">// Client (.csc)</span>
<span class="gsc-comment">// Detects field change -> Executes particle spawn.</span></code></pre>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div id="tab-ui" class="tab-panel hidden">
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                <p class="mini-kicker">Deprecation of .menu Files</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
                  The archaic <code class="gsc-inline-code font-mono text-accent">.menu</code> files from CoD5 have been completely deprecated. BO3 utilizes the modern <strong class="text-text-primary">Lua User Interface (LUI)</strong> frontend.
                </p>
                <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                  GSC scripts update frontend HUDs, Custom Perks, and Easter Egg trackers by piping data into <strong class="text-text-primary">UIModels</strong>. Lua scripts continuously listen to these models and dynamically animate/update the UI widgets on the screen.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <!-- Pitfalls -->
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl uppercase text-text-primary mt-8 mb-4">Top Migration Pitfalls</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-[linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(230,0,18,0.12)_0%,rgba(20,20,20,0.7)_100%)] border-accent/30">
                <p class="mini-kicker text-accent">G_Spawn Error</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                  Caused by hitting the entity limit. <strong class="text-text-primary">Fix:</strong> You must strictly call <code class="gsc-inline-code">ent delete();</code> on dynamic objects when done to prevent memory leaks.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30 border-border-light">
                <p class="mini-kicker">Undefined Linker Error</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                  Cannot find a function. <strong class="text-text-primary">Fix:</strong> BO3 requires explicit includes like <code class="gsc-inline-code">#using scripts\zm\my_script;</code> at the top of your file.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ── 5. Tutorials & Roadmap ── -->
          <section id="roadmap" data-guide-section class="surface-card rounded-sm p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24">
            <p class="section-kicker">Tutorials &amp; Roadmap</p>
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl uppercase text-text-primary leading-none mb-4">Best Tutorials &amp; Learning Roadmap</h2>
            <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
              The definitive, community-vetted path for a complete beginner to master BO3 GSC Mod Tools in 2026. Follow these ranked resources systematically.
            </p>

            <div class="space-y-4">
              <!-- Week 1 -->
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm overflow-hidden bg-charcoal/20">
                <button type="button" class="accordion-btn" data-accordion-btn>
                  <span>Week 1: Environment &amp; Lexicon</span>
                  <span class="accordion-icon">+</span>
                </button>
                <div class="accordion-panel" data-accordion-panel>
                  <div class="space-y-3">
                    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Set up the modern 2026 IDE toolchain and memorize GSC primitive data types.</p>
                    <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-4 bg-charcoal/40">
                      <span class="roadmap-badge roadmap-badge-guide">Guide</span>
                      <a href="https://wiki.modme.co/wiki/black_ops_3/guides/Scripting-guide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-primary hover:text-accent underline font-bold">NateSmithZombies Modme Scripting Guide</a>
                      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">&quot;COD script is a derivative of &apos;C code&apos;, with a lot of changes that make scripting easier.&quot;</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-4 bg-charcoal/40">
                      <span class="roadmap-badge roadmap-badge-tool">Tool</span>
                      <span class="text-text-primary font-bold">VS Code + vscode-gsc-ultimate Extension</span>
                      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">Ditch Notepad. Install Mjkzy&apos;s extension for static analysis and auto-completion of engine APIs.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </article>

              <!-- Week 2 & 3 -->
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm overflow-hidden bg-charcoal/20">
                <button type="button" class="accordion-btn" data-accordion-btn>
                  <span>Week 2 &amp; 3: World Interaction &amp; Event Logic</span>
                  <span class="accordion-icon">+</span>
                </button>
                <div class="accordion-panel" data-accordion-panel>
                  <div class="space-y-3">
                    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Master the Publisher-Subscriber event model, threading, and Radiant trigger links.</p>
                    <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-4 bg-charcoal/40">
                      <span class="roadmap-badge roadmap-badge-video">Video</span>
                      <a href="https://icegrenade.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-primary hover:text-accent underline font-bold">IceGrenade GSC Scripting Series (Parts 1-5)</a>
                      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">The absolute benchmark video series for linking triggers in Radiant map editor directly to backend GSC prints.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-4 bg-charcoal/40">
                      <span class="roadmap-badge roadmap-badge-video">Video</span>
                      <span class="text-text-primary font-bold">Program115 Scripting Series</span>
                      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">60+ video playlist covering practical implementations: playing FX, handling custom scoring overrides, and rotating entities.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </article>

              <!-- Week 4 -->
              <article class="surface-card rounded-sm overflow-hidden bg-charcoal/20">
                <button type="button" class="accordion-btn" data-accordion-btn>
                  <span>Week 4: Advanced Reverse Engineering</span>
                  <span class="accordion-icon">+</span>
                </button>
                <div class="accordion-panel" data-accordion-panel>
                  <div class="space-y-3">
                    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Decompile base game scripts to learn undocumented APIs and Treyarch&apos;s exact coding methodologies.</p>
                    <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-4 bg-charcoal/40">
                      <span class="roadmap-badge roadmap-badge-tool">Tool</span>
                      <a href="https://github.com/Scobalula/Cerberus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-primary hover:text-accent underline font-bold">Cerberus Decompiler (by Scobalula)</a>
                      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">Master-level essential tool. Decompiles .ff fastfiles back to GSC, bypassing FNV1A-64 hashes using smart loop detection.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ── 6. Content Ecosystem ── -->
          <section id="ecosystem" data-guide-section class="surface-card rounded-sm p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24">
            <p class="section-kicker">Content Ecosystem</p>
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl uppercase text-text-primary leading-none mb-4">Content Ecosystem Analysis</h2>
            <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
              The 2026 BO3 community landscape relies heavily on decentralized hubs. 90% of all online content is skewed towards Custom Zombies development rather than Multiplayer.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-start">
              <div class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl uppercase text-text-primary mb-4">Platform Utility Analysis</h3>
                <div class="guide-chart-container">
                  <canvas id="ecosystemChart"></canvas>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-text-muted text-center mt-3 italic">Analysis of platform utility based on 2024-2026 data trends.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="space-y-4">
                <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                  <p class="mini-kicker">Primary Hubs</p>
                  <h3 class="font-display text-xl uppercase text-text-primary mb-3">Discord Servers</h3>
                  <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                    Servers like <strong class="text-text-primary">Black Ops 3 Mod Tools (6k+ members)</strong> and Devraw discords are the ONLY places for real-time GSC debugging in 2026. <span class="text-accent">Drawback:</span> Knowledge is lost to chat history and unsearchable by Google.
                  </p>
                </article>
                <article class="surface-card rounded-sm p-5 md:p-6 bg-charcoal/30">
                  <p class="mini-kicker">Showcase &amp; Legacy</p>
